"1187","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1187 Arabic Hadees: 2356"
"1188","On the authority of Ibn Abbas that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: ""I saw tonight in a dream a canopy dripping with butter and honey, and I see people scooping from it — the one who takes much and the one who takes little. And there was a rope extending from the earth to the heaven, and I saw you take hold of it and ascend. Then another man took hold of it and ascended. Then another man took hold of it and ascended. Then another man took hold of it and it broke, then it was reconnected for him and he ascended."" Abu Bakr said: ""O Messenger of Allah! By my father and mother, let me interpret it."" The Prophet ﷺ said to him: ""Interpret it."" He said: ""As for the canopy, it is Islam. As for that which drips from it of honey and butter, it is the Quran, its sweetness dripping. So the one who takes much is the one who takes much of the Quran, and the one who takes little is the one who takes little. As for the rope extending from the heaven to the earth, it is the Truth which you are upon; you take hold of it and Allah raises you, then a man takes hold of it and rises, then another man takes hold of it and rises, then another man takes hold of it and it breaks for him, then it is reconnected for him and he rises."" He said: ""Inform me, O Messenger of Allah, by my father and mother! Did I get it right or wrong?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""You got some right and some wrong."" He said: ""By Allah, you must tell me what I got wrong."" He said: ""Do not swear."""""
